1.Explain the concept of Recurrent Neural Network. Describe why RNN is more suitable than 
traditional neural networks for sequential data.

RNN are neural network designed to handle sequential data (eg.time,series,text,speech).
They have loops that allow information to persist-meaning the output at time t depends on both the current input 
and previous hidden states.
Traditional feedforward networks treat inputs independtly, while RNN capture temporal dependencies and context across sequences.

