2.Differentiate between ANN, FNN, CNN, and RNN in terms of architecture and practical applications.

Model	                                Architecture	                      Practical Applications

ANN (Artificial Neural Network)	      Fully connected layers;             General classification/regression tasks
                                      no spatial or temporal structure	

FNN (Feedforward Neural Network)	    Data flows one way (no loops)	      Tabular data, simple predictions

CNN (Convolutional Neural Network)	  Convolution + pooling layers;       Image recognition, video analysis
                                      captures spatial patterns
                
RNN (Recurrent Neural Network)	      Recurrent connections;              Text generation, speech recognition,
                                      captures temporal patterns	        time-series forecasting

